{
  "component": "Radio Group",
  "description": "A labelled set of five Radio Field instances, available in horizontal and vertical layouts. The group label is editable text and each option carries a label row and a description row. PURPOSE: Lets a person pick one option from a short list of mutually exclusive choices under a shared heading such as \"Delivery speed\". BEHAVIOUR: Selection is single-choice, so picking one option clears the previous one. The group label names the question. Keyboard users move between options with arrow keys and the whole group takes one tab stop. COMPOSITION: Five instances of Radio Field per variant. Each Radio Field holds a \"Checkbox and Label\" frame and a \"Description Row\" frame. Code generators should look for an existing Radio Field or radio input in the codebase before building a new one, and reuse the group wrapper if one already exists. USAGE: Use when every option should be visible at once and only one answer is allowed. Use a select or dropdown when the list is long. Use checkboxes when more than one answer is allowed. The horizontal variant suits two or three short labels. The vertical variant suits longer labels or options with descriptions. CODE GENERATION NOTES: Render as a fieldset with the group label as the legend, and give every input the same name attribute so the browser handles single selection. The count of five is a Figma convenience, so treat options as data and map over them rather than hard-coding five items. Orientation should be a layout prop, not a separate component. Error, disabled and required handling sits on the group or the individual field and is not expressed as a Figma property here.",
